{
 "dur": 70.4,
 "vo": [
  {
   "id": "v01",
   "t": 0.4,
   "chunks": [
    "How was this",
    "train station built?",
    "46 St\u2013Bliss St stands",
    "on a concrete bridge",
    "from 1917."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02",
   "t": 7.09,
   "chunks": [
    "It started with",
    "the Dual Contracts of 1913:",
    "a plan to push the subway",
    "into Queens."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03",
   "t": 12.64,
   "chunks": [
    "The city wanted",
    "Queens Boulevard beautiful.",
    "So instead of a steel el,",
    "engineers chose",
    "reinforced concrete arches."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v04",
   "t": 19.54,
   "chunks": [
    "Footings went in first.",
    "Then crews poured concrete piers",
    "into wooden forms,",
    "around the clock."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v05",
   "t": 25.0,
   "chunks": [
    "Arches tied the piers together.",
    "Steel girders carried a deck",
    "for three tracks,",
    "with an express in the middle."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v06",
   "t": 30.89,
   "chunks": [
    "Then the station:",
    "two side platforms,",
    "canopies,",
    "and station houses",
    "tucked inside the viaduct."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v07",
   "t": 37.04,
   "chunks": [
    "On April 21, 1917,",
    "the 7 train rolled in."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v08",
   "t": 41.91,
   "chunks": [
    "In the fifties, the platforms grew",
    "for longer trains.",
    "But water seeped",
    "through the track bed,",
    "and the concrete crumbled."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v09",
   "t": 48.31,
   "chunks": [
    "From 1993 to '97,",
    "the viaduct was rebuilt:",
    "40,000 tons of concrete,",
    "new canopies,",
    "and stained glass."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v10",
   "t": 55.79,
   "chunks": [
    "In 2018,",
    "computer signals took over.",
    "Now it's being rebuilt again,",
    "with temporary platforms",
    "and two new elevators."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v11",
   "t": 63.23,
   "chunks": [
    "So, no grave yet.",
    "Congrats! You've discovered",
    "how 46 St\u2013Bliss St",
    "was built."
   ]
  }
 ]
}